ase tickets for a specific cultural event on a chosen date in a specified city.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"event_name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The official title of the event, such as an artist's name or a play title.\"\n        },\n        \"number_of_tickets\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"description\": \"The quantity of tickets to be reserved, must be an integer from 1 to 9.\"\n        },\n        \"date\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The date of the event, formatted as 'YYYY-MM-DD'.\"\n        },\n        \"city\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The name of the city where the event will take place, formatted as 'City, State' (e.g., 'New York, NY').\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"event_name\",\n        \"number_of_tickets\",\n        \"date\",\n        \"city\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"save_draft\",\n    \"description\": \"Save an email as a draft in the user's mailbox without sending it; recipients may be left empty.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"subject\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Subject line of the draft, copied exactly as the user gives it.\"\n        },\n        \"body\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Plain-text body of the draft, copied exactly as the user gives it.\"\n        },\n        \"to\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"description\": \"Recipient email addresses, in any order.\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Email address\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"subject\",\n        \"body\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Banking_1_CheckBalance\",\n    \"description\": \"Get the current and available balance of one of the user's bank accounts, in the account currency.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"account_type\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Which of the user's accounts to use.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"checking\",\n            \"savings\"\n          ],\n          \"default\": \"checking\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": []\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: How much is in my savings account?\n\nReply with only a JSON array of the tool calls that fulfil the request, each of the form {\"name\": \"<tool name>\", \"arguments\": {...}}, where \"arguments\" is a JSON object (not a string). When the request needs several calls, list them all. Reply with [] if no tool fits the request, or if the request does not give a value for a required argument: never guess one. Include every required argument. Include an optional argument only if the request asks for a value for it; otherwise leave it out and the tool applies its default. Give each value the type its schema declares: JSON numbers for integer and number, true or false for boolean, and strings for string, copied exactly as written.","role":"user"},{"content":"[{\"name\":\"Banking_1_CheckBalance\",\"arguments\":{\"account_type\":\"savings\"}}]","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool results:\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Banking_1_CheckBalance\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"account_type\": \"savings\",\n      \"balance\": 3721.55,\n      \"currency\": \"EUR\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: Move 1062 of it to NL72BANK0938098303, reference \"Rent March\".\n\nReply as before: only a JSON array of tool calls, or [] if no tool fits or a required value is missing.","role":"user"}]